Spire Zero: an AI that learned Slay the Spire 2 from zero

An AI inside the game, for single-player runs:
[list]
[*][b]Advice[/b]: at every decision it shows what it would do, and each option's chance to win the run.
[*][b]Auto-play[/b]: on request it plays a step, the rest of a turn or a room, or keeps going until you pause it.
[/list]
Nobody wrote any part of how it plays, and it learned nothing from human games: it learned all of it from runs it played itself. At each decision it tries the options on a copy of the game, then asks a learned network how likely the run is to be won from where each one leads.

[h2]Two modes (in the settings)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]SL[/b] (the default): like saving and loading, it tries the options on a true copy of the room you are in, so it sees what will really happen there (the draw order, the random rolls). It cheats, and it plays at its strongest.
[*][b]NoSL[/b]: only what a player can see. No peeking.
[/list]

[h2]How well it plays[/h2]
In SL, on test seeds, the share of runs it won:
[table]
[tr][th][/th][th]Ascension 0[/th][th]Ascension 10[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]The Ironclad[/td][td]98% (49/50)[/td][td]41.5% (83/200)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]The Silent[/td][td]86% (43/50)[/td][td]30.5% (61/200)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]The Defect[/td][td]98% (49/50)[/td][td]34% (68/200)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]The Regent[/td][td]94% (47/50)[/td][td]22% (44/200)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]The Necrobinder[/td][td]90% (45/50)[/td][td]15.5% (31/200)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]The Fool[/td][td]57.5% (115/200)[/td][td]0.5% (1/200)[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]The game at exactly [b]v0.113.1[/b], Steam's [b]public-beta[/b] branch (the game's Properties, then Betas). On another version the mod turns itself off and says why.
[*]Windows (x64), Linux (x64) or macOS (Apple silicon).
[*]Single-player only.
[/list]

[h2]What it runs on your computer[/h2]
While the game runs, the mod starts its own brain, a background program where the AI thinks, on half of your logical processors (at most 8). It ends when the game does. There is nothing else to install.

[h2]Source and design[/h2]
